1. `When don't know how many number of elements will be given for input` : 
    use while `(cin >> x) {// code}` 
    

2. `In some contests files are used for input and ouput` : An easy solution for this is 
    to write the code as usual using standard streams, but add the following lines to the 
    beginning of the code: `freopen("input.txt", "r", stdin);freopen("output.txt", "w", stdout);
    `  `After this, the program reads the input from the file “input.txt” and writes the output
    to the file “output.txt”.` 
